---

Touched 2026-10-16 to force a pull of the current GitHub main.

The Communications Center lands with twelve new edge functions. Every one of
them answered 404 from the functions gateway before this merge, which is the
expected state for code that has only ever lived on a branch - but it is also
exactly what the 2026-09-21 entry below describes for functions that were
already on main and still had not deployed, so the two cases look identical
from outside. These are the twelve to check:

  comms-journey-actions          comms-whatsapp-config
  comms-mailchimp-api            comms-whatsapp-status-webhook
  comms-mailchimp-webhook        comms-whatsapp-templates
  comms-process-journeys         meta-api
  comms-twilio-balance           meta-oauth-callback
  meta-oauth-start               meta-token-refresh

A 404 after the build means the sync skipped it. 401 is the healthy answer for
the JWT-protected ones: the function is live and refusing an unauthenticated
call. Only three are reachable from the UI today - comms-whatsapp-templates,
comms-whatsapp-config and comms-twilio-balance - so those are the ones a 404
would actually be visible on, as an error in place of data on the WhatsApp
Templates and Config pages and in the wallet balance card.

supabase/config.toml also gains verify_jwt = false for five of them
(the two webhooks, the Meta OAuth callback and the two cron entry points);
worth confirming that came across too, since a webhook that silently keeps
JWT verification fails closed and looks like Twilio or Mailchimp being quiet.
